    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d186">

                <pb facs="0457" n="373" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg373"/>

                <head>No. 182.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L. West to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-03-24"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 24</date>.
                        [Received March 25.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 23d instant, in reply to mine of the 19th, informing me
                    that, as full and formal public notification in the premises has already been
                    given by the President’s proclamation of the 31st January, 1885, it has not been
                    found necessary to give to United States fishermen any further notification that
                    they are now precluded from fishing in British North American territorial
                    waters. I have duly informed Her Majesty’s Government and the Government of the
                    Dominion of this decision.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>L. S. SACKVILLE WEST.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
